# Google Drive: "Open from Google Drive". Copy to .env and fill in; the
# Drive buttons are hidden unless all three are set. These are read at build
# time and end up in the public JavaScript, which is normal for them: the
# OAuth client is locked to its authorized JavaScript origins and the API key
# should be restricted to those websites and the Google Picker API.
#
# Google Cloud console (one project):
#   1. Enable "Google Picker API" and "Google Drive API".
#   2. OAuth consent screen: External; add the scope .../auth/drive.file.
#   3. Credentials > OAuth client ID > Web application. Authorized JavaScript
#      origins: https://rendicahya.github.io and http://localhost:5173
#   4. Credentials > API key. Restrict it to those websites and to the
#      Google Picker API.
#   5. The project number is on the project's dashboard (IAM & Admin > Settings).
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=
